# 🚀 Node.js Application

The application exposes the following endpoints:

```text
GET /
GET /health
GET /metrics
```

### Application Port

```text
3000
```

Access the application using:

```text
http://<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>:3000
```

---

# 📊 Application Metrics

The Node.js application exposes metrics through:

```text
/metrics
```

Example:

```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/metrics
```

## HTTP Metrics

The application collects metrics such as:

* Total HTTP requests
* HTTP request duration
* HTTP response status codes
* Request methods
* Request latency

Example metrics:

```text
http_requests_total
http_request_duration_seconds
```

## Node.js Runtime Metrics

The application also exposes runtime metrics, including:

```text
nodejs_heap_size_total_bytes
nodejs_heap_size_used_bytes
nodejs_eventloop_lag_mean_seconds
nodejs_gc_duration_seconds
process_cpu_user_seconds_total
process_resident_memory_bytes
```

These metrics help monitor the health and performance of the Node.js application.

